{"schemaVersion":2,"id":"practice-专项-source-8a7d06e069d3","kind":"practice","title":"【未上传】试题部分WORD—5年高考、3年模拟_专题十三细节理解（可作答题）","year":"专项","region":"资料","variant":"可作答资料","instructions":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"专题十三　细节理解"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"【5年高考】"}]}],"sections":[{"id":"section-legacy","title":"旧卷综合题型","instructions":[],"layout":"flow","groups":[{"id":"group-legacy","instructions":[],"stimulusBlocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"A组　统一命题·新高考卷、课标卷题组"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Passage 1　　主题语境:人与社会　　词数:222　　限时:6分钟"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"　　(2021新高考适应卷,A)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Non-Credit Courses"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"The Pre-College Program offers non-credit courses. Students will experience college-level courses given by some of our college's leading experts and will receive written feedback (反馈)on their work at the end of the course. Pre-College students will also receive a grade of Satisfactory/Unsatisfactory and a certificate of completion at the conclusion of the program."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"All non-credit courses meet from 9:00 a.m.—11:30 a.m. daily and may have additional requirements in the afternoons or evenings."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"COURSE:Case Studies in Neuroscience"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"·June 11—July 2"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"·Leah Roesch"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Using student-centered, active-learning methods and real-world examples, this course is designed to provide a fuller understanding of how the human brain works."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"COURSE:Psychology of Creativity"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"·June 15—June 28"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"·Marshall Duke"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Why are certain people so creative? Is it genetic(遗传的),or a result of childhood experience? Are they different from everyone else? This popular psychology course highlights the different theories of creativity."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"COURSE:Creative Storytelling"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"·June 21—July 3"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"·Edith Freni"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"This college-level course in creative storytelling functions as an introduction to a variety of storytelling techniques that appear in different forms of creative writing, such as short fiction and playwriting."}]}],"sharedOptions":[],"questions":[{"id":"q-1","displayNumber":1,"sourceQuestionNumber":1,"type":"single_choice","promptBlocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Who is the text intended for?"}]}],"placement":{"kind":"standalone"},"options":[{"id":"A","label":"A","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"The general public."}]}]},{"id":"B","label":"B","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"College freshmen."}]}]},{"id":"C","label":"C","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Educational experts."}]}]},{"id":"D","label":"D","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"High school students."}]}]}],"blanks":[],"answerSpec":{"availability":"answered","gradingMode":"auto","kind":"choice","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"normalization":{"unicodeNfkc":true,"trim":true,"collapseSpaces":true,"caseSensitive":false}},"explanationBlocks":[],"sourceRefs":[{"sourceDocumentId":"8a7d06e069d34c8674f145264c398ad64c57c07f339268cf5da9a67271195074","relativePath":"题型/【未上传】试题部分WORD—5年高考、3年模拟_专题十三细节理解.docx","sha256":"8a7d06e069d34c8674f145264c398ad64c57c07f339268cf5da9a67271195074","locator":{},"extractionMe